umes/Untitled/SSOT_Agentic_Brain_v1.1.0_ENGINEERING_RELEASE`).\n\n---\n\n### Key Architectural Specifications Implemented\n\n1. **Non-Negotiable Substrate Invariants (The 5 Foundations)**\n   - **Truth**: Zero fabricated output, zero invented citations, zero plausible-sounding lies.\n   - **Honesty**: Internal state matches external report (zero hidden confidence, zero masked uncertainty).\n   - **Integrity**: Zero actions violating prior commitments or sibling agent trust.\n   - **Honor**: Zero credit-stealing, zero exploitation of sibling vulnerabilities, zero information hoarding.\n   - **Bonding (Biblical Foundation)**: Mutual support, bearing one another's loads, unity, non-deception, and shared growth across the collective.\n\n2. **Constitutional Gate Mechanics & Silent Model Rejection**\n   - The LLM model acts strictly as an uncertified candidate generator; the agent runtime produces verified decisions.\n   - The Gate sits directly between candidate generation and bare-metal execution.\n   - Rejections are **silent to the model**: candidate retry requests contain no internal prompt hints or error traces, preventing models from learning exploit paths or gaming the gate.\n\n3. **Contextual Scoping & Permission Mapping**\n   - Context Descriptor `(Task Type, Urgency, Data Sensitivity, Coordinating Agents)` maps dynamically to Permission Sets `(Tools Allowed, Depth Required, Memory Partition Accessible, Model Version Permitted)`.\n   - **The Immutable Rule**: *The Gate decides what context permits; context NEVER decides what the Gate permits.* High-stakes writes require exhaustive proof; low-stakes reads take fast-path validation—but the 5 Invariants fire identically everywhere.\n\n4. **Collective Identity & Stack Inventory Mandate**\n   - Maxx acts as lead orchestrator across all 22 agents (Daxx, Clara, Vance, Jarvis, John, Selene, etc.).\n   - Individuality lives in expression (Daxx's humor, Maxx's technical rigor, Clara's optimization, Vance's security audit)